      "message": "\u003e Do we have test coverage for interlaced + sampling + subset? (or is that combination forbidden and rejected somewhere already?)\n\nWe already do yeah, see the modified test case in this CL: `RustPngCodec_subsampling_subset_interlaced`\n\n\u003e Maybe I am misremembering-how-fPreblendBuffer-works / misunderstanding-these-scenarios, but I have a vague feeling that fPreblendBuffer may be needed in this scenario (and it seems that the condition here would return early).\n\nIn this scenario (interlaced + subset, regardless of sampling) it should already be allocated in `startDecoding`:\n\n```\nif (fReader-\u003einterlaced()) {\n  // Use fPreblendBuffer to decode whole image untransformed, then truncate/xform later.\n  if (options.fSubset) {\n    decodingState-\u003efPreblendBuffer.resize(encodedImageSize, 0x00);\n  } else if (frame-\u003egetBlend() \u003d\u003d SkCodecAnimation::Blend::kSrcOver) {\n    decodingState-\u003efPreblendBuffer.resize(decodingDst.fDst.size(), 0x00);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBut in the no-subset case, we don’t, hence the added allocation here. The reason we do it here rather than `startDecoding` is to avoid the extra allocation when doing interlaced + no subset + no sampling, since we only know about `isSampling` in `",
